<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;m still very early in my GTA VI experience — Chapter One — a prologue that sets the standard for a 10+ hour tutorial for one of the best games you&#8217;ll ever play. Two brief thoughts:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">First, prior to GTA, I&#8217;ve been an avid <a href="https://randsinrepose.com/archives/the-one-about-arc-raiders/">ARC Raiders</a> player during my long post-<a href="https://randsinrepose.com/archives/ten-reasons-to-play-destiny/">Destiny</a> depression. Whether you like extraction shooters or not, you can&#8217;t argue the game is gorgeous. There are times I just want to wander around on one of those maps. GTA is that level of detail, except it&#8217;s a mind-boggling open world with fewer killer robots. I&#8217;ll go further: it&#8217;s the most realized open world I&#8217;ve ever experienced. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Second, one of the games I play while playing is &#8220;I wonder if&#8230;&#8221; For example, there are iguanas everywhere. I stood at the side of the road as one of the iguanas ran across the road, and I thought, &#8220;I wonder if&#8230; the iguana will be killed.&#8221; It was.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Immersion is broken when you play I-wonder-if, and it fails to meet your expectations. GTA meets all I-wonder-if expectations and usually exceeds them.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">But, yeah, there are a few bugs.</p>


